# AI provider keys — the terminal alternative to pasting a key into Settings.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in whichever provider you use. The Vite dev
# server reads these in Node and attaches them as requests leave the proxy, so
# the key is never sent to the browser, never stored in localStorage, and never
# visible in dev tools.
#
# You only need one. Anything set here takes precedence over a key entered in
# the Settings panel, and Settings will show that it is being used.
#
# Restart `npm run dev` after changing this file — it is read at startup.
#
# `.env` is gitignored. Never commit real keys.

# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...

# Production builds only: route provider calls through your own proxy instead
# of calling vendor hosts directly from the page. See README > Deployment.
# VITE_API_PROXY=https://your-proxy.example.com
